Z||000000||Oreif||05-14-2000||08:03 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SideV_1.jpg"> <P>Here is a pic I took today of my car with the new KYB/Eibach lowered suspension. I am going to the GT Diamond spoke wheels and 50 series tires as soon as I refinish them. (they have been stripped now I just need to paint and polish them!)<P>How's it look?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||05-14-2000||08:57 PM||||I think Cartman said it best..<P>"sweeeeet..."<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Coconut||05-14-2000||09:11 PM||||oreif, she looks damn good! Now you've got me thinking about lowering my ride too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Job well executed!    ||||reg||1
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||05-14-2000||09:24 PM||||Looks Great !!! But I have a couple of questions. 1. How does it effect handling ? 2. How does it effect ride quality ?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||05-14-2000||09:29 PM||||Oreif, that looks goooood, I was also thinking or lowering, A friend of mine just had his done Friday I took him to the shop to pick it up, it's an 85 coupe I looked at it real good but couldn't picture mine with the Areo fascsa  NOW I SEE ! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks, He had the springs cut the shop said it was about 1 3/4<BR>and it may drop the other 1/4 after it seats. I did not talk to him over the week end to ask about the feel/ride.<P>How does your ride/feel?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sillhouette.com||05-14-2000||10:07 PM||||Sorry for this but being a new guy around here I found it interesting that among so many fiero enthusiasts lowering is not a standard thing.  The very first mod to my fiero was lowering springs with urethane busings KYB struts and rear sway bar.  I don't know how good the handling is since I've only driven a fiero that was lowered and modified I do know that there is no car out there that can outhandle the fiero.  I have first hand knwledge on MR2 new corvette, mustangs, grand prix, and many more.  These are some of the more impressive handlers out there that I supprised on an off or on ramp.  <P>Later<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||05-14-2000||10:26 PM||||Dale and DXR_DAD, The poly bushings improve steering. I think taking the flex out of the control arms gives it a more positive feel. The Eibach springs are very stiff. The car handles like it's glued to the road. The ride is very stiff but not annoying. The reason I am going to 15" 50's is the 235/60HR14's on the car tend to roll onto the sidewall in hard cornering. The sidewall right now is 5.6" going to 245/50HR15 my sidewall will decrease to 4.8" and my overall diameter by 1/2" Which will lower the car another 1/4". When you first do lower it like I did it is a weird feeling when the car barely leans in a hard turn. But oh so nice!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Cutting the stock springs will lower it but I have heard that the suspension will bottom out more often.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Homicidal||05-14-2000||11:00 PM||||How much does a lowering job cost?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||05-14-2000||11:06 PM||||Total cost for my upgrades which include, suspension kit (KYB struts/shocks, Eibach springs, and KONI sway bars with poly bushings), Poly Bushings, new ball joints and new tie rods, new bearings and rotors, and brake pads, was $1100.00 Just the suspension kit was $620 The brakes and bearings were another $310 and the rest was bushings and ball joints.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||05-14-2000||11:11 PM||||Hey Oreif, can it tear-up the tires?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>auto, right?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||05-14-2000||11:17 PM||||Yes it's an auto, Slight squeel from dead stop very very slight chirp from first to second (shift kit is installed)||||reg||1
Z||000011||2birds||05-15-2000||12:07 AM||||Oreif,<BR>It looks great.  Watch the front tire size now that you've lowered it.  215/60/15 rubs at full lock.  I'd like to hear how 50-series works for you.<BR>Are the springs variable or linear rate?  I have linear rate Suspension Technique Springs and poly bushings on mine, and they're pretty rough on the kidneys.  I ordered the variable rate Eibachs with Tokico shocks/struts for my 97 T-bird, and I'm wondering what to expect.||||reg||1
Z||000012||frontal lobe||05-15-2000||02:31 AM||||Looks beautiful!  I like the rims you have on.  Would like to see a picture of the new rims on side-by-side to this pic to compare the look!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||05-15-2000||09:20 AM||||The 50 series tires I am going to are smaller then the 60 series you mention. Right now I have 234/60HR14's and I'll be going to the 245/50HR15's<P>Tire size  -  sidewall  -  width  -   radius   -  circum<BR>245/50-15  -  4.8 in  -  12.3 in  -  24.6 in  -  77.4 <BR>225/50-15  -  4.4 in  -  11.9 in  -  23.9 in  -  75.0 <BR>215/60-15  -  5.1 in  -  12.6 in  -  25.2 in  -  79.0 <BR>235/60-14  -  5.6 in  -  12.6 in  -  25.1 in  -  78.9 <P>My springs are the Eibachs. They are very firm but it doesn't feel like your riding on a rock. I rode in a car with the KONI race set-up and it war very hard.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||05-15-2000||09:56 AM||||Oreif--'85 GT or '86 SE???  Looks umm...OK.  What am I saying?  Damn, that's a sweet car! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyone know the drawbacks (other than possibly bottoming out) of cutting the springs?  I'd like to lower the Grape Ape, but just can't swing the cash to do it right.  Cut springs would only be temporary (maybe until next summer).  Any thoughts???||||reg||1
Z||000015||Big O||05-15-2000||10:32 AM||||Great looking car.  I went that route with my GT 3.8 Series II but found the ride quality was just too harsh for my old bones.  I had BFG Comp T/A 245/45ZR16 tires all the way around.  I found that this size was just too wide and the sidewal was just too stiff.  I drove like it was glued to the road, but the rear wheel clearance ate one of the tires before I could get them off.  I finally wound up removing the Eibachs and trading them in for a set of stock springs.  I replaced the BFG's with a nice set of Pirelli 4000 tires and the ride quality greatly improved.  Still great handling, but a lot less harsh on the front suspension.  Six months with the stiff suspension and my whole front end was starting to come unglued.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Flash Box||05-15-2000||10:59 AM||||Oreif, Nice looking car. <P>(I just realized that your name is Fiero spelled backward)||||reg||1
Z||000017||LAMBO||05-15-2000||12:04 PM||||Oreif, that what I hope my '85 grows up to look like (with a few differences, of coarse). Job well done!||||reg||1
